==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɒt|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{m|en|grotto|}}, by shortening, or {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|grotte}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|poetic}} A [[grotto]].
#* '''1819''', {{w|John Keats}}, ''[[s:La Belle Dame sans Merci|La Belle Dame sans Merci]]'':
#*: She took me to her elfin '''grot''', / And there she wept, and sigh'd full sore, / And there I shut her wild wild eyes / With kisses four.

===Etymology 2===
{{back-form|grotty|lang=en}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~|grots}} {{tcx|British|lang=en}}

# {{lb|en|slang|uncountable}} Any [[unpleasant]] substance or material.
# {{lb|en|slang|countable}} A miserable person.

